# Deadlines Page (Calendar & List) - Cursor Rule

## Summary of Recent Changes
- **Modal Improvements:**
  - Modal now syncs with `initialData` for editing.
  - Modal width and button layout improved for responsiveness.
- **Card & Button Layout:**
  - Action buttons (check, notes, edit) are always bottom-right, spaced, and never overlap content.
  - Type/category info and action buttons are separated with max vertical spacing.
- **Check Mark Logic:**
  - Card greys out when completed, but check mark remains vibrant.
- **Notes:**
  - Notes tooltip appears top-left of the button.
  - Notes popup Cancel button matches the Add Item modal style.
- **Calendar/List Synchronization:**
  - Clicking a list item sets the calendar date (month/week/day) to the item's date, respecting the current view.
  - Clicking a calendar event scrolls to and highlights the corresponding list item.
  - Highlighted list item is visually marked.

## APIs Needed
- **Deadlines CRUD:**
  - `GET /api/deadlines` - Fetch all deadlines for the user
  - `POST /api/deadlines` - Create a new deadline
  - `PUT /api/deadlines/:id` - Update a deadline
  - `DELETE /api/deadlines/:id` - Delete a deadline
- **Notes:**
  - `PATCH /api/deadlines/:id/notes` - Update notes for a deadline
- **Google Calendar Sync:**
  - `GET /api/google-calendar/auth` - Get Google Calendar auth URL
  - `POST /api/google-calendar/sync` - Sync deadlines with Google Calendar

## Future Notes
- Consider accessibility for keyboard navigation and screen readers (focus management, ARIA roles for modals/tooltips).
- If deadlines list grows large, consider virtualization for performance.
- Highlighting logic is currently in-memory; if multi-user or multi-tab sync is needed, persist highlightedId in state or URL.
- If more actions are added to cards, revisit button layout for mobile responsiveness.
- For recurring deadlines, ensure backend supports recurrence rules and correct expansion.
- See [page.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/app/deadlines/page.tsx) for main implementation.
